    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math learning by adapting explanations to individual strengths and weaknesses, addressing my preference for structured, logic-based approaches. They could also bridge gaps left by traditional teaching, like providing deeper context or interactive problem-solving exercises. For me, the key would be ensuring these tools align with my analytical mindset while being flexible enough to accommodate my low openness to new ideas."
